    "summary": "High‑energy US Festival set with scorching China Cat>Rider and Shakedown",
    "review": "The September 5, 1982 Glen Helen show captures the Dead at full festival throttle. The band bursts out of the gate with a turbo‑charged Playing In The Band → Shakedown Street segue that never lets up, rolling into a ripping New Minglewood Blues and a blistering China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider that sets the night on fire. Set two keeps the momentum with a spacey Space → Not Fade Away stretch, solid Sam­son & Delilah, and classic closers – Black Peter, Sugar Magnolia, U.S. Blues and a rollicking Satisfaction. Jerry’s lead work is soaring, Brent’s keyboards add adventurous color (despite occasional distortion), and Bill’s drumming drives the whole thing with tight, dynamic power. Multiple soundboard sources capture this high‑octane performance, but the Miller SBD (gd1982-09-05.sbd.miller.113746.flac16) stands out for its crisp balance after a brief low‑end wobble and its faithful rendering of the band’s fireworks.",
